-->
<workout_file>
    <author>Tom Jelen</author>
    <name>HIIT 4x4</name>
    <activitySaveName>High Torque: HIIT 4x4 min ~120% FTP @ 60-70 rpm</activitySaveName>
    <description>The HIIT session from Hebisz and Hebisz (2024, PLoS ONE), weeks 1–4 volume: four 4-minute intervals at 60–70 rpm with 8 minutes of active rest between them. Seated throughout. The study set the intervals at 90–100% of maximal aerobic power (Pmax) and the rest "at an intensity similar to the power achieved at VT1" (the first ventilatory threshold). It gives no FTP. ~120% FTP is my estimate: in the paper's baseline values VT2 is about 75% of Pmax, so 90–100% of Pmax is ~120–136% of VT2, and I take FTP as roughly VT2 and use the bottom of that range. This is the most uncertain number in the library. ~65% FTP for the rest is my estimate the same way (VT1 is about 65% of VT2). The study riders rode outdoors uphill; this is an indoor adaptation at %FTP targets. The two short openers (30 s at normal cadence) are my addition, not from the study.</description>
    <sportType>bike</sportType>
    <tags />
    <workout>
        <Warmup Duration="900" PowerLow="0.40" PowerHigh="0.75">
            <textevent timeoffset="5" duration="15" message="Warm up at your normal cadence. No low cadence until the first interval." />
            <textevent timeoffset="30" duration="30" message="This session comes from a 2024 study by Hebisz and Hebisz: 4x4 min at 90-100% of maximal aerobic power, 60-70 rpm, 8 min active rest. Its first four weeks." />
            <textevent timeoffset="75" duration="20" message="All the research behind this program: high-torque.jelen.dk" />
            <textevent timeoffset="120" duration="30" message="The study gave no FTP numbers, so ~120% is an estimate. If it feels far too hard or far too easy, adjust the workout intensity." />
            <textevent timeoffset="360" duration="25" message="Today's cadence is 60-70 rpm, not lower. The study kept these longer intervals a bit higher than its sprints." />
            <textevent timeoffset="480" duration="30" message="Stay seated for every interval. Coach Neal Henderson's reason: seated riding puts less compression on your joints." />
            <textevent timeoffset="600" duration="20" message="If your knees ache at any point during an interval, stop the interval. Don't push through knee discomfort." />
            <textevent timeoffset="720" duration="30" message="Tired today? Lower the workout intensity. The study did something similar: on mornings when a rider's heart-rate variability was low, that day's HIIT was ridden much easier." />
            <textevent timeoffset="840" duration="20" message="Two short openers at normal cadence first. Then the main intervals." />
        </Warmup>

        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="1.10">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Opener 1. Normal cadence." />
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.55">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Easy spin. Second opener coming." />
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="1.10">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Opener 2." />
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.55">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" duration="25" message="Last easy spin before the main set. In ERG mode, just drop to 60-70 rpm when the interval starts. The trainer holds ~120% FTP." />
            <textevent timeoffset="90" message="30 seconds. First interval. STAY SEATED throughout." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="1.20" Cadence="65">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="STAY SEATED. 60-70 rpm. ~120% FTP. GO." />
            <textevent timeoffset="20" message="Hard by design. Legs and lungs." />
            <textevent timeoffset="60" message="1 minute in. Hold the cadence." />
            <textevent timeoffset="120" message="Halfway. 2 minutes to go. Do not spin up." />
            <textevent timeoffset="180" message="Last minute. Stay seated." />
            <textevent timeoffset="210" message="30 seconds. Do not stand." />
            <textevent timeoffset="230" message="10 seconds." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="480" Power="0.65">
            <textevent timeoffset="2" message="Active rest. 8 minutes at ~65% FTP." />
            <textevent timeoffset="40" duration="25" message="Tip: if you can't hold the power at this cadence, lower the workout intensity a few percent rather than grinding." />
            <textevent timeoffset="120" duration="30" message="Fact: in the study, the low-cadence group's VO2max rose about 9% and their maximal aerobic power about 8%. The normal-cadence group: about 4% and 3%." />
            <textevent timeoffset="300" message="Knee check. Any discomfort that feels joint-related, not muscle burn?" />
            <textevent timeoffset="450" message="Next interval in 30 seconds. Seated. 60-70 rpm." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="1.20" Cadence="65">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="STAY SEATED. 60-70 rpm. ~120% FTP. GO." />
            <textevent timeoffset="20" message="Interval 2. Legs and lungs." />
            <textevent timeoffset="60" message="1 minute in. Hold cadence." />
            <textevent timeoffset="120" message="Halfway. 2 minutes to go. Do not spin up." />
            <textevent timeoffset="180" message="Last minute. Stay seated." />
            <textevent timeoffset="210" message="30 seconds. Do not stand." />
            <textevent timeoffset="230" message="10 seconds." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="480" Power="0.65">
            <textevent timeoffset="2" message="Active rest. 8 minutes." />
            <textevent timeoffset="60" duration="30" message="The study riders did these outdoors, uphill on 6-9% grades. Indoors at a set power is the Zwift version." />
            <textevent timeoffset="240" duration="25" message="At 250 W FTP, ~120% at 65 rpm is about 44 Nm of torque on each pedal stroke." />
            <textevent timeoffset="450" message="Interval 3 in 30 seconds. Seated. 60-70 rpm." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="1.20" Cadence="65">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="STAY SEATED. 60-70 rpm. ~120% FTP. GO." />
            <textevent timeoffset="20" message="Interval 3. Third of four." />
            <textevent timeoffset="60" message="1 minute in. Same again." />
            <textevent timeoffset="120" message="Halfway. 2 minutes. Hold cadence." />
            <textevent timeoffset="180" message="Last minute. Stay seated." />
            <textevent timeoffset="210" message="30 seconds. Do not stand." />
            <textevent timeoffset="230" message="10 seconds." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="480" Power="0.65">
            <textevent timeoffset="2" message="Active rest. One more to go." />
            <textevent timeoffset="60" duration="20" message="The study went to 6 reps in weeks 5-8. Four is where it started." />
            <textevent timeoffset="240" duration="20" message="If your knees are aching, skip the final interval. Protecting the joints is always the right call on torque work." />
            <textevent timeoffset="450" message="Last interval in 30 seconds. Seated." />
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="1.20" Cadence="65">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="STAY SEATED. 60-70 rpm. ~120% FTP. GO. Final interval." />
            <textevent timeoffset="20" message="Last one." />
            <textevent timeoffset="60" message="1 minute in. Three minutes to go." />
            <textevent timeoffset="120" message="Halfway. Do not spin up. Do not stand." />
            <textevent timeoffset="180" message="Last minute." />
            <textevent timeoffset="210" message="30 seconds. Finish it." />
            <textevent timeoffset="230" message="10 seconds." />
        </SteadyState>

        <Cooldown Duration="900" PowerLow="0.50" PowerHigh="0.40">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Four intervals done. Spin easy at normal cadence." />
            <textevent timeoffset="150" duration="25" message="Note how your knees feel. Any ache? If it keeps coming back, stop torque work and see a professional." />
            <textevent timeoffset="360" duration="30" message="One small study: well-trained women aged 17-20, 12 per group. The paper reports no knee or injury monitoring. Promising, not proven." />
            <textevent timeoffset="540" duration="25" message="Leave at least a full day before your next torque session. No back-to-back days." />
        </Cooldown>
    </workout>
</workout_file>
